Subject: Add samples after using nimbleMCMC
Message-ID: <pXtUDYMb2N0.Uoxy0duJAQAJ@nimble-users.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/nimble-users/c/pXtUDYMb2N0/m/Uoxy0duJAQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Is it possible to add more samples after running a model using nimbleMCMC? For example, is it possible to add more samples to "mcmc.output" after the initial 20,000 samples were run and convergence wasn't reached yet?
Thanks for the great program.
Jay

code <- nimbleCode({
    mu ~ dnorm(0, sd = 1000)
    sigma ~ dunif(0, 1000)
    for(i in 1:10) {
        x[i] ~ dnorm(mu, sd = sigma)
    }
})
data <- list(x = c(2, 5, 3, 4, 1, 0, 1, 3, 5, 3))
inits <- function() list(mu = rnorm(1,0,1), sigma = runif(1,0,10))

mcmc.output <- nimbleMCMC(code, data = data, inits = inits,
                          monitors = c("mu", "sigma"), thin = 10,
                          niter = 20000, nburnin = 1000, nchains = 3,
                          summary = TRUE, WAIC = TRUE)

