Yes, this functionality is certainly available in the NIMBLE MCMC, but not via the high-level convenience function nimbleMCMC(), nor using runMCMC().

You'll need to use the slightly longer (and much more customizable) workflow:

Rmodel <- nimbleModel(code, constants, data, inits)
conf <- configureMCMC(Rmodel)
Rmcmc <- buildMCMC(conf)
Cmodel <- compileNimble(Rmodel)
Cmcmc <- compileNimble(Rmcmc, project = Rmodel)
Cmcmc$run(niter = 10000)
samples <- as.matrix(Cmcmc$mvSamples)

Then, you can continue running the same MCMC for, say, an additional 50,000 samples, picking up right where it left off, by using the reset = FALSE argument:

Cmcmc$run(niter = 50000, reset = FALSE)
samples_extended <- as.matrix(Cmcmc$mvSamples)

I'm sure this is documented in the NIMBLE User Manual <https://r-nimble.org/manuals/NimbleUserManual.pdf>, as well.  Let me know if you have any questions.

Daniel

